WEBVTT

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.860
The Hanno Alps?

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:38.870
Apparently there's a mountain 
range from Mt. Tenran to Chichibu,

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:41.750
and they're called the Hanno Alps.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:42.930
Wow!

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.500
I think I'll go check it out tomorrow.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.500
<i>Sorry, I'm going for a drive 
with my family tomorrow.</i>

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.740
Oh...

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:51.960
That's okay.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.000
<i>Will you be all right going by yourself?</i>

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.320
It's close by.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.010
I'll be fine.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:02.180
I've been to Mt. Tenran and 
Mt. Tohnosu past that.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:03.410
<b>Mt. Tenran</b>

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:03.410
<b>Mt. Tohnosu</b>

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.520
I think I'll try climbing 
from Mt. Tenkaku next.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.520
<b>Mt. Tenkaku</b>

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:10.920
I get off at Higashi-Agano Station, 
and go from Mt. Tenkaku to Mt. Otaka.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.780
It'll be a good opportunity 
to break in my hiking shoes.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.780
Take care.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.990
Here, take some rice balls.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.670
Thanks.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:27.660
It's heavy!

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.190
They're huge!

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.290
I made some for Hinata-chan, too.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.410
<i>I'm going by myself, though...</i>

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:38.530
<i>But Mom would worry if I told her that.</i>

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.680
I'll see you!

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.200
<b>Mt. Tohnosu</b>

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.970
It's heavy, but this is probably 
perfect for getting in shape.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.970
<b>Mt. Tenran</b>

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.450
<i>Right.</i>

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:52.480
<i>I have to gain experience and stamina 
for next year's trip up Mt. Fuji.</i>

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:56.030
<i>I wonder what the Hanno Alps are like.</i>

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.480
<i>I can't wait!</i>

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.490
<b>Alps in Hanno?!</b>

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.150
I made it!

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.870
Higashi-Agano Station!

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.370
There...

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.080
So heavy...

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.630
But this is part of my training!

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:22.130
Mt. Tenkaku
Yugate
Kohburi Pass
Kitamuki-Jizo - Lake Kamakita

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:22.130
Mt. Tenkaku is this way... Right.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.640
What's Yugate?

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.390
Yugate

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.640
Mt. Tenkaku

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.640
Trails with Stories

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.390
Mt. Tenkaku

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.010
Good.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.910
It's so cool.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.670
Mt. Tenkaku Peak

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.670
Sawasuji Course - One Course

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.670
Sawasuji Course and One Course?

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:59.970
One Course is drawn as a dotted line, 
which means it's a difficult trail.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.010
I think I'll take the Sawasuji Course.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.850
It's so quiet here.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.020
There's no one around.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:20.730
That's right.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.030
I'm alone right now.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:28.030
I can choose everything, 
including which courses I take.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:32.360
Walking fast, walking slow...

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.290
I can walk at my own pace.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.050
Everything is as I please!

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:42.010
This entire mountain belongs to me!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:47.300
The call of shooting stars...

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.310
At the glissades...

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:59.780
Will I find that person, 
holding a flower in their mouth?

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:11.810
My heart's excited...

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:17.590
The nostalgic climbers...

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:20.090
I can't read it.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.950
This is the right way, isn't it?

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:26.090
There's no one around to ask.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.280
Up we go.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.610
I'm glad I brought my gloves.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:51.700
My feet are fine thanks to my new 
shoes, but my backpack's so heavy.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.640
There.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.390
Higashi-Agano Station | Mt. Tenkaku Peak

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.700
Kusumi Pass via Higashi Pass

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.950
<b>The Mt. Tenkaku
Protection Association</b>

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.740
<b>Mt. Tenkaku</b>

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.740
Please take your garbage with you

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.650
I'm exhausted.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.480
This is no fun.

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:42.250
Maybe I'll just go home...

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:56.970
I miss you, who are so smooth...

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:00.270
I can't wait to see you...

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:00.270
Am I hearing things?

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:04.370
My serow...

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:05.900
Am I seeing things?

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.650
What? Aoi-san?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.120
Kokona-chan?

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.530
Are you all right?

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.780
I-I'm fine.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.010
I was just taking a break.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:19.670
Thank goodness.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.540
I thought you had passed out.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.290
Wh-What a coincidence this is.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:25.310
Yes!

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.800
I'm here to see serows.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.910
Which way did you come from?

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:33.330
I came up the Sawasuji Course.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:36.050
I came up the One Course.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:39.960
It's like I'm riding on Muma-kun's back.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:45.510
There was a nice Muma-kun bench, 
and cute signs and things.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:46.570
Watch for Snakes

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.960
Really?

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.530
What are you doing after this?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.170
Going home...

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:56.580
I was thinking of going to Mt. Otaka.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.650
May I come with you?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.330
Mt. Tenkaku

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.330
S-Sure, of course!

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:08.330
Thanks for holding my bottles.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.840
It's okay.

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:16.090
So you were training for Mt. Fuji, huh?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:19.350
Although I already passed 
out at Mt. Tenkaku.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.420
You're making great progress 
if you've found your limit.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.200
You think so?

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.820
Now you just have to overcome 
it in your training.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.320
I see.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.440
<i>It's convincing when Kokona-chan says it.</i>

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.860
<b>Mt. Tenran
<- Left</b>

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.860
<b>Right</b>

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.370
Are those your new hiking shoes, Aoi-san?

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.850
Yeah, I took the plunge.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.300
They're very nice.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:51.720
You got yours from your mom 
on your birthday, right?

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.130
Yes!

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.160
Kokona-chan, Kokona-chan!

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.270
A serow mother and baby!

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:21.160
<i>It was nice coming up here alone, 
but it's still more fun being with someone.</i>

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.400
Mt. Tenran      Nenogongen 
Mt. Otaka

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:28.170
Rice ball bombs!

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.910
Thank you!

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:31.050
It's okay.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.970
These are too big to eat two on my own.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.180
Pickled plum!

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.030
It really hits the spot when you're tired.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.430
You're right! It's so good!

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.230
Tell your mom I said thanks.

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.440
Okay!

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.690
<i>I was only planning to come this far, but...</i>

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.920
Want to walk a little farther, Kokona-chan?

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.390
I'd love to.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:00.700
Oh, yeah. There's a nice place up ahead.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.450
A nice place?

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.750
Nenogongen

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.270
Look at that amazing cedar tree.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.840
Over here, Aoi-san.

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.410
These Deva king statues are so colorful.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.850
They're so cute.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.970
<b>Nenogongen Tenryu Temple</b>

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.970
Nenogongen Tenryu Temple?

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:27.100
Yeah.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.230
These things.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.480
What are these? Straw sandals?

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:36.490
Nenogongen enshrines the god 
of leg and back protection.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:40.970
"Demon fire can hurt your back and legs.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:44.990
Offerings

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:47.030
Those with injuries from their hip 
down must pray with sincerity."

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:50.060
In other words, pray to the gods here,

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:53.000
and they'll protect you 
from injuring your legs.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:57.510
I wanted you to make it 
here if you're training.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:02.260
So that you can make it to Mt. Fuji 
without getting hurt next year.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:05.260
Yeah!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:14.680
<i>I pray that I may make it to 
the top of Mt. Fuji this time.</i>

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.320
Tokyo Skytree View

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.130
It's so nice.

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:24.240
Yes.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:27.400
<i>It was painful and exhausting,</i>

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:30.360
<i>but none of that matters when 
you make it to the goal.</i>

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:34.330
Thanks for coming with me, Kokona-chan.

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.730
It was fun.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:38.590
Don't mention it. I had fun, too.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:43.440
<i>The Hanno Alps were surprisingly tough.</i>

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:48.600
<i>But I walked lots and gained just 
a little more confidence, I think.</i>

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:51.370
<i>To be continued.</i>

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:55.500
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:59.940
So what was "Yugate," anyway?

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.940
Yugate
